				"relight": "Take another coal from Homecoming's cresset.",
				"arrive": "You carry the rim's coal to the Stair's foot, and lay it in the lamp-post's basket. Far up on the Crowns, very faintly, a bronze mouth turns a hair toward the village. It is only the wind.",
				"text": "Carry the rim's coal down to Hearthward and the Stair's foot. Walk it: a run, a roll, a blow or deep water puts it out"},
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(-1.5, 17.6), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The Stair's foot",
				"text": "Read the Stair's foot for Brannoc's forty ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "forty", "at": Vector2(-3.9, 19.2), "name": "the forty small bells", "text": "Forty small bells of Brannoc's casting, hung up the Stair at every hundred steps, bronze, a hand tall. The lowest hangs here, at the foot, with a bit of blue ribbon on it. Its voice, when the wind lifts it, is not a note but a small, helpless child's cough."},
					{"key": "ledger", "at": Vector2(-1.5, 20.0), "name": "a casting ledger", "text": "Brannoc's ledger on a hook: FORTY. LAST CAST THE WEEK BEFORE. I HEARD THEM, ALL FORTY, ON THE NIGHT, STOPPING, ONE AT A TIME, FROM THE TOP. I WAS AT THE FOOT. I COUNTED. I DO NOT THINK I HAVE EVER STOPPED."},
					{"key": "stone", "at": Vector2(0.9, 20.8), "name": "a footprint in stone", "text": "A footprint worn into the Stair's lowest step, left, very deep, by someone who stood a long time and then went up. It is the exact size of the wanderer's, and has been here for nine winters."},
